      "note": "The New Zealand waste disposal levy, quoted per tonne as the published figure is. The formula divides by 1000 rather than the constant being pre-converted, so that the number a staff member types matches the number the legislation states." }
  ],
  "formulas": [
    { "metric": "co2e", "expression": "qty_kg * (upstream + downstream)",
      "notes": "The default shape, present for contrast." },
    { "metric": "water", "expression": "min(qty_kg * upstream, 500000)",
      "notes": "A cap, which is the shape a staff member reaches for first after the default. The cap BINDS on this case's quantity - the uncapped value is 1259190 - so a min() that returned its first argument would fail here." },
    { "metric": "cost", "expression": "round(qty_kg * (upstream + downstream + const_LEVY_NZD_PER_T / 1000), 2)",
      "notes": "Every part of section 4.3's language the other eight cases never touch: a function call, a division, and a constant inside a parenthesised sub-expression. round(x, 2) in particular is what the admin panel advertises, so it is the first thing staff will type." }
  ],
